_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Normalize a `null` repo before building the links.**

The default parameter on line 67 applies only when `repo` is `undefined`. The CLI supplies `null`. `readFlag` in `scripts/sentry/autofix/sentry-autofix-finalize.mjs` (lines 710-716) returns `null` for an absent flag, and line 853 forwards that value as `refusedInventoryRepo`. The usage text on lines 690-691 documents `--refused-inventory-repo` as optional.

If the flag is omitted, every rendered link becomes `https://github.com/null/issues/<n>`. The count stays correct, so the defect is silent and lands on the public tracker comment.

<details>
<summary>🔗 Proposed fix to validate the repository argument</summary>

```diff
-export function renderRefusedStubInventory(
-  refusedInventory,
-  repo = REFUSED_INVENTORY_DEFAULT_REPO,
-) {
+export function renderRefusedStubInventory(refusedInventory, repo) {
   const inventory = parseRefusedStubInventoryResult(refusedInventory);
   if (inventory.state !== "known") {
     return "- Refused stubs (all states): unknown";
   }

+  // The CLI passes null for an absent optional flag, which a default
+  // parameter does not catch. Validate the owner/name shape instead.
+  const target =
+    typeof repo === "string" && /^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/.test(repo)
+      ? repo
+      : REFUSED_INVENTORY_DEFAULT_REPO;
   const links = inventory.issues.map(
-    (number) => `[#${number}](https://github.com/${repo}/issues/${number})`,
+    (number) => `[#${number}](https://github.com/${target}/issues/${number})`,
   );
```

Add a test that omits the repository argument and asserts the default owner/name appears in the links.
</details>

